ibe each class. Prospectus disclosure typically addresses:\n\n- **Dealing:** exchange trading versus primary-market subscriptions and redemptions at NAV\n- **Settlement:** exchange settlement cycles versus fund settlement timing\n- **Costs:** fees, charges, and any dealing or spread costs\n- **Minimums:** minimum subscription and holding amounts\n- **Rights:** voting, information, and redemption rights of each class\n- **Liquidity:** secondary-market liquidity versus direct redemption access\n- **Price differences:** market price versus NAV, including premiums and discounts\n\nTreat this as a general outline, not the specific requirements of Q&A 1088.","ttft_ms":2469,"type":"result","duration_ms":4039,"uuid":"9487ab30-3d1b-452c-b5e6-71f88acc315a","ttft_stream_ms":427,"time_to_request_ms":58,"first_content_frame_ms":427,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
